{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And Moses wrote.</b> He wrote the place they journeyed to and the place they journeyed from, for sometimes the place they arrived at was for the purpose of harm, while the place they departed from was good." "<b>And these were their journeys by their starting points.</b> And sometimes the opposite occurred. He also recorded the nature of each journey — that it involved departing from one place to another without prior notice, which was very difficult, yet despite this they did not refrain. Therefore it is written for each one, וַיִּסְעוּ מִמָּקוֹם פְּלוֹנִי וַיַּחֲנוּ בְּמָקוֹם פְּלוֹנִי (they journeyed from such-and-such a place and encamped at such-and-such a place), for each journey and each encampment was difficult."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:41:38.602136542Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}